customer: activist_guy
daypart: afternoon
brief:
	He has seen what happens and leaves town. He just leaves his computer and leaves, without a problem: "I would recommend you stay away from tech as well." Digging deep in it finds his research. With a lot of time: he has downgraded his OS. His narrative ends here.

== drop-off
(neutral) Dude.
- What?
- Are you ok? You look a little...
(irritated03) Listen. The bogon flux around here is off the charts. Do what I'm doing. Pack up and leave.
- Uuh...
- I can't really leave. I promised to take care of the store this week.
	(irritated02) Forget the store.
- What do you mean "bogon flux"?
	(irritated02) It's in the computers. Something's spreading, box to box.
	- Spreading how?
		(irritated03) I don't have time to explain. Figure it out.
	- Yeah, I've been noticing some strange things myself.
		(irritated01) We're running out of time.
(irritated02) I would be halfway to the coast by now if I hadn't come by to warn you. Just scram already. (irritated03) Or don't, for all I care!
- Okay, thanks for the heads up. What about your computer?
	(neutral) I always help when I can. About the computer... (angry) You can keep it - I'm planning on staying away from any tech for the foreseeable future.
	- Okay...? Stay safe, I guess!
